# Typos and misspellings -- the case the character-trigram space is genuinely good at.
#
# Kept as its own kind because it is the one class where the shipped vectoriser should
# beat a word-level or sentence-level model rather than lose to it. Measured on this
# corpus, "inflation" against "inflatoin" overlaps 38% in the trigram space; a model that
# cannot reach these is not an upgrade even if it doubles paraphrase recall, and the
# reason for keeping the fusion rather than replacing the lexical half wholesale.

[typo-en-001]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: inflatoin
expect: e4293295-fb43-46b0-7ac5-08dec461c23d
why: Two characters transposed in the shortest name in the corpus.

[typo-en-002]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: obesety rate
expect: 6825244a-5e9b-428e-85cf-08ddb7179f3f
why: One vowel wrong.

[typo-en-003]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: populaton
expect: 160100bc-528f-4622-bc88-08de9e09a558
why: A dropped character in a common word.

[typo-en-004]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: hopsital beds
expect: 966b1cac-bff0-4d5a-7abe-08dec461c23d
why: A transposition in the distinguishing word.

[typo-en-005]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: occupancy rate of hotles
expect: 4f2dc17c-83dd-427a-7ab5-08dec461c23d
why: A transposition at the end of the last word.

[typo-en-006]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: greenhouse gaz emissions
expect: 6836f2fa-f1c8-4023-7ab2-08dec461c23d
why: A phonetic misspelling.

[typo-en-007]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: logistics performence index
expect: b60f7e11-c096-4fab-64ce-08de064080f9
why: A misspelling inside a long published name.

[typo-en-008]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: watr consumption
expect: 9cc91459-7e8e-4ec2-870b-08dee641c19a
why: A dropped vowel.

[typo-en-009]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: gross national incom
expect: fb801dff-2204-4cbb-7aaf-08dec461c23d
why: A truncated final word.

[typo-en-010]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: internatonal visitors
expect: 7bd4d5a6-a5b9-4a63-7ab3-08dec461c23d
why: A dropped character mid-word.

[typo-en-011]
lang: en
kind: typo
question: smokin rate
expect: 1367abb3-a507-4b3f-85d0-08ddb7179f3f
why: A dropped final consonant, which is also how the word is spoken.

[typo-ar-001]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: التضحم
expect: e4293295-fb43-46b0-7ac5-08dec461c23d
why: خ written as ح -- adjacent letters, one dot apart. The published Arabic name is two words long, so a single wrong letter is a large fraction of the whole surface.

[typo-ar-002]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: معدل السمنه
expect: 6825244a-5e9b-428e-85cf-08ddb7179f3f
why: Teh marbuta written as a plain heh -- the single commonest Arabic misspelling there is, and one AD-26's fold is expected to absorb rather than one the vector space must.

[typo-ar-003]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: عدد الاسره في المستشفيات
expect: 966b1cac-bff0-4d5a-7abe-08dec461c23d
why: Alef without its hamza and a teh marbuta as heh, both in one question.

[typo-ar-004]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: استهلك المياه
expect: 9cc91459-7e8e-4ec2-870b-08dee641c19a
why: A dropped alef turns the noun استهلاك into a verb. Finding 42's morphology arriving as a typo rather than as a paraphrase.

[typo-ar-005]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: معدل اشغال الفنادق
expect: 4f2dc17c-83dd-427a-7ab5-08dec461c23d
why: The hamza dropped from إشغال.

[typo-ar-006]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: الناتج المحلي الاجمالي
expect: fc6dccb5-e101-48bd-6a30-08dea2389ab1
why: الإجمالي written without its hamza -- published both ways elsewhere in this very export, which is why the fold decides it and not the reader.

[typo-ar-007]
lang: ar
kind: typo
question: عدد السياح من خارج الدوله
expect: 7bd4d5a6-a5b9-4a63-7ab3-08dec461c23d
why: Teh marbuta as heh on the final word.
